# What an image build of this repository may see — written as an allow-list:
# everything is kept out, then the few paths a build needs are let back in.
# A path that is not named here never reaches a build context, so nothing a
# build cannot see can be copied into a published image: no .env file, no
# .claude/ session state, no edge-function secrets. (Images are published by
# CI from a clean checkout; this is what makes a local build match it.)
#
# The images are in sylou-local/; each adds only the paths it needs.

*

# The Sylou Local web image (sylou-local/web/Dockerfile): the app as Vite
# builds it, from the committed lockfile.
!.npmrc
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!index.html
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.app.json
!tsconfig.node.json
!src
!public

# The image's own files. Letting one folder back in takes three lines: the
# parent, everything in it out again, then the one folder that may be seen.
!sylou-local
sylou-local/*
!sylou-local/web

# Hosted Sylou's header file for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify: a package
# install would serve it as a plain file, and its own headers come from
# sylou-local/web/nginx.conf.
public/_headers

# Kept out whatever a line above re-included, because these must never reach
# a build: the last matching pattern wins.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.claude
